@@ -206,6 +206,16 @@ The owner saw the haze flicker in the trailer's dawn shot ("Moving out at dawn",
 - **Fix.** psFogInject turns the frame's jitter per cell with an interleaved-gradient offset of the cell, and in depth also per slice, so neighbouring cells' residuals are independent and average out. The sequence, the history share and the uniforms are unchanged. New test `[remaster][fog][Shaders]`.
 - **Result.** Valley band on the reshot clip: 0.567 to 0.103, 25076 spikes to 2 (vanilla 0.112). In play at 60 fps: 0.308 to 0.112. The look is unchanged apart from a hair more mist. Fog cells with no history (after a camera cut) may show cell-size speckle for a few frames; not seen in the clips.
 
+## F2. The fog wind (2026-10-23)
+
+The F1 fix stopped the pump, but the owner saw "motion in the fog that makes it look like wind is blowing through it". Eight Opus agents and three Fable agents worked on a shared board (`graphics-remaster/tmp/video/fogwind/`, not in git) and judged motion explicitly: x-t slices of the camera-compensated residual, the velocity of the frame-difference pattern, a probe with the camera held still, and real-time 60 fps recordings, besides block flicker.
+
+- **Cause.** The F1 offset of a cell, interleaved gradient noise, is a ramp over the cells: one cell to the right adds 0.556 of a slice. The frame's golden-ratio step adds 0.618 (0.570 and 0.755 in xy), so each frame's offset field was the last one read about one cell over. The history's residual therefore slid through the fog about one 12 px cell per frame, in every region, held camera or panning, in play and in the captures: blotches 2 to 4 cells across, about 700 px/s. Any per-cell offset that is a lattice-periodic or linear function of the cell plus a frame-wide step translates the same way. A white per-cell hash does not travel but boils in place (2x the floor in play).
+- **The amplifier.** The history was read at the frame's jittered point, so the stored value was a leaky sum of the offsets (gain 1 / 0.12, about 8) instead of their average. Read at the cell's centre, the original frame-wide pump alone fell 9x.
+- **Fix.** psFogInject samples each cell at two fixed points (depth strata at a quarter and three quarters of the slice, each weighted by the metres of its half slice, on the diagonal quarter points of the cell; `VolumetricFog.hpp` kFogTapZ, kFogTapXY) and never jitters them. The history is read at the cell's centre through a fixed tetrahedral blur of a quarter cell and slice (kFogHistoryBlur, [1 6 1] / 8 per axis), the mean of the blur the jittered read used to give the stored volume, which is the mist's softness in the approved look. The jitter uniforms stay 0; the frame count still steps the near field's march. The medium is unchanged, so AI sight still matches the drawn fog. Test `[remaster][fog][Shaders]`: a mirror of the injection and its history over a cell grid measures the pump (the swing of a 5 x 5 block's mean), the travel (the correlation of one frame's residual change with the last frame's at a non-zero cell lag) and the stillness with the camera held; the frame-wide offset trips the pump bar, the F1 gradient the travel bar (held and panning), the fixed taps neither and stand exactly still.
+- **Result.** The dawn shot reshot on the fixed build (agent 1's kit on the clip, frames 240 to 390, against vanilla's and F1's shots of the same path): wind over bay / valley / far hill / haze 0.005 / 0.004 / 0.002 / 0.004 (vanilla 0.017 / 0.011 / 0.002 / 0.003, F1 0.061 / 0.162 / 0.104 / 0.060), the residual's travel correlation at most 0.04 (F1 0.22 to 0.38 at 12 px a frame), band 0.077 (vanilla 0.103, F1 0.093, the original 0.516), valley block flicker 0.074 (vanilla 0.062, F1 0.121, the original 1.63). With the camera held: travel 0.47 to 0.03, in-place change 0.42 to 0.05 code values (the jitter-frozen floor 0.08), valley block flicker 0.11 to 0.02. In play at 60 fps (the same shader as a live override on the recorder build): held-camera boil 0.42 to 0.06, travel under the pan at most 0.03. The look stays within about one code value of the approved one (valley mean +0.6 in motion, 128.2 against 128.1 in play). Cost: one more medium and light sample per cell and three more history fetches, +0.09 ms on the air stage at 1080p (two uncontended pairs of the held-camera probe: 0.70 and 0.70 ms before, 0.79 and 0.78 after).
+- **Ruled out.** A white per-cell hash alone (boils like F1); white in time (boils 1.8x more); blue-ish per-cell phases (no gain); a history-free far field (2x the block flicker under a pan: the column light steps as horizon-ring bins enter and leave view); 8 taps (no gain over 2); taps spread to tent quantiles (no look gain). Equal on every instrument but not chosen: a strictly periodic 8-frame cycle (needs a new uniform, keeps a 7.5 Hz pattern at 60 fps, slower at low frame rates), a 2x2 antithetic pattern with a display tent, and 2 to 4 jittered taps; the fixed taps leave nothing temporal at any frame rate or capture cadence.
+
